// StorageProvenance — which roots a value may share a record with, and where a call stores what it was handed.
//
// A `return` retains a borrow rather than copying it, so a call's result may be a second reference to what
// its caller handed over: an argument, a receiver, a capture, a payload. A call may also STORE what it was
// handed — into another argument, into module storage, into its result — or BIND it to a mutable name. E3078
// and E3159 ask of a VALUE what the parser asks of a name it can see. One trace per function ranks its roots —
// its parameters (the summary's bit order) then module `var` storage, or its `let` bindings in declaration
// order, then the parameters, then writable storage — and each value carries a set per column over them:
//
// | set | the value may … the root's record | read by |
// |---|---|---|
// | `identity` | be | E3078, E3159, the parameter-mutation edges |
// | `inside` | lie within, read out of it | E3078 |
// | `placedWithin` | lie within, stored into it | the summary |
// | `holds` | contain, in a field no load can name | a load, whose `identity` it becomes |
// | `storedHolds` | contain, stored into it by this body (field-exact through `storeSlots`) | a load |
// | `deepHolds` | contain inside a record it contains | a load, whose `holds` it becomes |
// | `storedDeep` | contain inside, stored there through a record lying within it | the summary |
// | `holdsWithin` | contain a record lying within | a load, whose `inside` it becomes |
// | `shares` | overlap, at any depth | a caller, deciding whether a summary relates it to an argument |
//
// ⭐ **E3078 ASKS `identity` AND `inside`, NOT WHAT A VALUE HOLDS** — a `var` may not BE a `let`'s
// record or lie within one, which are the two shapes `Parser.requireMutableBindingSource` refuses
// by name (`var b = a`, `var i = o.inner`). A `var` that merely CONTAINS one was handed it by a
// store or a kept argument, and that is the door that asks (`decideMutablePlaceStore`,
// `refuseKeptLetArgument`): a fresh `let` moves into writable storage at its last use, and any
// other immutable value is refused there.
//
// ⭐ **A READ OUT OF A `var`'S STORAGE MAY BE A `let`'S RECORD.** A `let` stored into a `var`'s
// record or module `var` storage leaves its rank on what the storage holds, and a door counts that
// rank only while the `let` is live (`rootCountsAtDoor`): a read out of such storage — a load, a
// call that may hand back what its argument holds — is what the storage holds, as a read out of any
// root is, and it also lies within the storage. A read out of a PARAMETER's record takes only what
// this body stored into that field (`storeSlots`): what the caller's record held is the caller's to
// judge, at its own doors, and a parameter's fields are rebound under the body's own reads
// (`view old = states` then `states = fresh`).
//
// ⭐ **A VALUE READ OUT OF A ROOT AND ONE STORED INTO IT BOTH LIE WITHIN IT, AND ONLY THE FIRST MAY BE WHAT
// ELSE IT HOLDS.** `inside` says the value came out of the root, so a call handing it back may hand back
// anything the root contains; `placedWithin` says it was put there, which is all it says — else a function
// that registers a record and returns it (`addBlock`) would return everything its registry holds.
//
// ⭐ **A STORE IS FIELD-EXACT FOR THE VALUE IT WENT INTO.** A store into `box` at offset k is filed under
// `(box, k)`, and a load of `box` at offset k reads exactly those — so writing a `let` into one field of a box
// does not make every other field of it that `let`. Only the value itself is exact: a name derived from it
// carries what was stored into it collapsed (`storedHolds`), since its fields are no longer the box's. A store
// a CALL makes names no field, so it lands in `holds`, which every load reads.
//
// ⭐ **CLOSED BY DEFAULT.** A value is fresh only where the ownership model says so
// (`IrFunction.valueMintedSole`), and a callee whose body was read answers through its summary — a witness
// dispatch, or a call through a function value, through the summary of every body it may land on. Every other
// op that defines a value — a runtime entry, an op added later — may be any record reachable from its operands
// (`maxonOpOperandValues`), and a call with no summary may store what it was handed wherever
// `runtimeCalleeStoreShape` does not rule out. A new door is refused until proven fresh, never the reverse.
//
// ⭐ **WHAT A SET CANNOT TYPE, THE TYPES DO.** A root set collapses fields and depths, so a door asks it only of
// roots the value's type admits: a record of another type is not the root's own (`valuesMayBeOneRecord`), and
// one of a kind the root's type cannot hold does not lie within it (`ProgramSignatures.recordKindsWithinAggregate`).
//
// ⭐ **EVERY RECORD A MODULE-LEVEL `let` HOLDS IS ONE MORE ROOT, PAST WRITABLE STORAGE (`moduleLetRank`).** A parameter
// trace reads it off a `let`'s slot and files what its result is to it in the summary's `moduleLets`, so a caller that
// names no `let` still learns that a call handed one back — which is what E3078 refuses a `var` initializer and E3159
// a write through. Being one such record is asked with the `let`s' record kinds, since the rank collapses them all.
//
// ⚠ **ONE SET PER VALUE FOR THE WHOLE BODY**: what a value may be is gathered over every op of the
// body, in no order. Only liveness is ordered, by the token of the door asking (`askAtDoor`): a
// `let` counts at a door it is bound before and read after, a `view` at every door past its
// declaration, a module-level `let` at every door. The doors themselves are tabled above
// `beginStorageDoors`.

typealias MaskWordCount = int(0 to u64.max) implements ElementIndex
typealias MaskWordCountArray = Array with MaskWordCount

enum RootLinkSlot
	setHead
	chunkLink
end 'RootLinkSlot'

enum RootLinkState
	unlinked
	linked
end 'RootLinkState'

typealias RootLinkStateArray = Array with RootLinkState

enum RootRankLookup implements Error
	noRoot
end 'RootRankLookup'

// A store's field, as one key: the address value in the high word, the byte offset in the low one.
typealias StoreSlotKey = int(0 to u64.max) implements ElementIndex
typealias StoreSlotKeyArray = Array with StoreSlotKey

typealias RootSetIdArray = Array with ElementIndex

// Two buckets per entry keeps the chains at about one hop. Both are powers of two, so a bucket is a mask.
let StoreSlotBucketsPerEntry = 2 as ElementIndex
let StoredKeyParameterName = b"key"
let StoredElementParameterName = b"element"
let IteratorInterfaceName = b"Iterator"
let FirstStoreSlotBuckets = 16 as ElementIndex

// The address value spread by an odd multiplier before the byte offset joins it: the fields of one record
// share an address and differ only in the offset, so an unmixed key would file them all in one bucket.
let StoreSlotAddressSpread = 131

enum StoreSlotLookup implements Error
	unfiled
end 'StoreSlotLookup'

// ⭐ **ONE WALK'S FIELD-EXACT SETS, BY THE WHOLE `(address, offset)` KEY.** A body reaches many fields
// through one address, so chaining by ADDRESS alone walks every field's slot at every store and a record
// literal of K fields costs K². MEASURED on one, `phase:semanticCheck` CPU per doubling of K at K = 1,600 →
// 6,400: ×2.89 ×3.40 chained by address, ×1.77 ×2.04 keyed by the whole key. Reset empties only the buckets
// this walk filled, so starting a walk costs the last walk's entries and never the table's size.
export type StoreSlotTable
	var buckets as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var keys as StoreSlotKeyArray
	var slots as RootSetIdArray
	var nexts as OptionalElementIndexColumn

	export static function create() returns StoreSlotTable
		return Self{buckets: OptionalElementIndexColumn.create(), keys: StoreSlotKeyArray.create(), slots: RootSetIdArray.create(), nexts: OptionalElementIndexColumn.create()}
	end 'create'

	export function reset()
		for entry in 0 upto self.keys.count() 'eachFiled'
			let key = try self.keys.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.reset: keys.get OOB at {entry}")
			self.buckets.clear(self.bucketOf(key))
		end 'eachFiled'

		self.keys.clear()
		self.slots.clear()
		self.nexts.makeAbsent(0)
	end 'reset'

	module function entryCount() returns ElementIndex
		return self.keys.count()
	end 'entryCount'

	module function entryAt(entry ElementIndex) returns (ValueId, ElementIndex, ElementIndex)
		let key = try self.keys.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.entryAt: keys.get OOB at {entry}")
		return (storeSlotAddress(key), storeSlotOffset(key), try self.slots.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.entryAt: slots.get OOB at {entry}"))
	end 'entryAt'

	function setAt(key StoreSlotKey) returns ElementIndex throws StoreSlotLookup
		var entry = try self.headAt(key) otherwise throw StoreSlotLookup.unfiled

		while (try self.keys.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.setAt: keys.get OOB at {entry}")) != key 'eachFiled'
			entry = try self.nexts.get(entry) otherwise throw StoreSlotLookup.unfiled
		end 'eachFiled'

		return try self.slots.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.setAt: slots.get OOB at {entry}")
	end 'setAt'

	function file(key StoreSlotKey, slot ElementIndex)
		self.spreadOverMoreBuckets()
		let entry = self.keys.count()
		let bucket = self.bucketOf(key)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.slots.push(slot)
		self.chainOnto(entry, bucket: bucket)
	end 'file'

	function chainOnto(entry ElementIndex, bucket ElementIndex)
		if let head = try self.buckets.get(bucket) 'aChain'
			self.linkNext(entry, to: head)
		end 'aChain' else 'theFirstInTheBucket'
			self.endChainAt(entry)
		end 'theFirstInTheBucket'

		self.buckets.set(bucket, value: entry)
	end 'chainOnto'

	function linkNext(entry ElementIndex, to ElementIndex)
		if entry < self.nexts.count() 'refiled'
			self.nexts.set(entry, value: to)
			return
		end 'refiled'

		self.nexts.push(to)
	end 'linkNext'

	function endChainAt(entry ElementIndex)
		if entry < self.nexts.count() 'refiled'
			self.nexts.clear(entry)
			return
		end 'refiled'

		self.nexts.pushAbsent()
	end 'endChainAt'

	// Twice the buckets whenever the next entry would crowd them, re-linking what this walk has filed. The
	// entry columns keep their order, so only the chains are rebuilt.
	function spreadOverMoreBuckets()
		if (self.keys.count() + 1) * StoreSlotBucketsPerEntry <= self.buckets.count() 'roomEnough'
			return
		end 'roomEnough'

		let wider = FirstStoreSlotBuckets if self.buckets.count() == 0 else self.buckets.count() * 2
		self.buckets.makeAbsent(wider)

		for entry in 0 upto self.keys.count() 'eachFiled'
			let key = try self.keys.get(entry) otherwise panic("StoreSlotTable.spreadOverMoreBuckets: keys.get OOB at {entry}")
			self.chainOnto(entry, bucket: self.bucketOf(key))
		end 'eachFiled'
	end 'spreadOverMoreBuckets'

	function headAt(key StoreSlotKey) returns ElementIndex throws AbsentError
		if self.buckets.count() == 0 'nothingFiled'
			throw AbsentError.absent
		end 'nothingFiled'

		return try self.buckets.get(self.bucketOf(key))
	end 'headAt'

	function bucketOf(key StoreSlotKey) returns ElementIndex
		let mask = (self.buckets.count() - 1) as StoreSlotKey
		let mixed = (storeSlotAddress(key) as StoreSlotKey) * StoreSlotAddressSpread + storeSlotOffset(key)
		return (mixed and mask)
	end 'bucketOf'
end 'StoreSlotTable'

typealias NamedTypeRecordMemo = Map with (TypeNameId, bool)

// What may lie within a record of an aggregate or an instance — asked of every immutable root of every walk
// (`ProgramSignatures.recordKindsWithinAggregate`).
typealias AggregateRecordKindsMemo = Map with (ByteArray, HeldRecordKinds)
typealias InstanceRecordKindsMemo = Map with (GenericInstanceId, HeldRecordKinds)
typealias HeldRecordKindsArray = Array with HeldRecordKinds

// One mask per parameter of a function: which of its parameters its body stores into that one's record.
module typealias ParamMaskRows = Array with ParamPositionMaskArray

// Positions into another column: its entries, or the start of each group of them.
module typealias EntryIndexArray = Array with ElementIndex

// The byte offset a field read steps by.
typealias AccessStep = int(0 to u64.max)
typealias AccessStepColumn = OptionalIndexColumn with AccessStep
typealias MergingBlockColumn = OptionalIndexColumn with BlockId

// One step of an access path: a field read at its offset, or an element of a container.
union PathStep
	field(offset AccessStep)
	element

	function fieldOffset() returns AccessStep throws AbsentError
		match self 'step'
			field(offset) then return offset
			element then throw AbsentError.absent
		end 'step'
	end 'fieldOffset'
end 'PathStep'

typealias PathStepArray = Array with PathStep

let MaxAccessPathSteps = 32 as ElementIndex

typealias HygieneIndexByPosition = Map with (PositionKey, ElementIndex)
typealias MoveSiteIndexArray = Array with ElementIndex

// The token a root is taken to be moved at when no door moved it: past every token of any body. A door asking
// about every root, moved or not, asks before the first token.
let NeverMovedToken = u64.max as ElementIndex
let NoDoorToken = 0

typealias KeptSiteHeadsByCall = Map with (PositionKey, ElementIndex)

let FirstToken = 1 as ElementIndex

// One refusal a door made, held until the function's doors have all asked so they report in source order.
type PendingRefusal
	export let at as PositionKey
	export let line as LineNumber
	export let column as ColumnNumber
	export let code as ErrorCode
	export let message as String

	static function create(line LineNumber, column ColumnNumber, code ErrorCode, message String) returns PendingRefusal
		return Self{at: positionKey(line, column: column), line: line, column: column, code: code, message: message}
	end 'create'
end 'PendingRefusal'

typealias PendingRefusalArray = Array with PendingRefusal

enum KeptContent
	ofItsOwnType
	typeParameterOnly
end 'KeptContent'

type PendingKeep
	export let value as ValueId
	export let holders as ParamPositionMask
	export let destination as ValueId
	export let content as KeptContent

	static function create(value ValueId, holders ParamPositionMask, destination ValueId, content KeptContent) returns PendingKeep
		return Self{value: value, holders: holders, destination: destination, content: content}
	end 'create'
end 'PendingKeep'

typealias PendingKeepArray = Array with PendingKeep

enum KeptMark
	escapes
	returned
end 'KeptMark'

type VarDeath
	export let rank as ElementIndex
	export let until as ElementIndex

	static function create(rank ElementIndex, until ElementIndex) returns VarDeath
		return Self{rank: rank, until: until}
	end 'create'
end 'VarDeath'

typealias VarDeathArray = Array with VarDeath

union KeepDestination
	unknown
	within(record ValueId)
end 'KeepDestination'

function moveKindHandsTheVarOver(kind MoveDestinationKind) returns bool
	return match kind 'kind'
		letField or
		letPayload or
		readOnlyElement gives true
		mutableName or
		letFieldValue or
		letPayloadValue or
		readOnlyElementValue or
		keptArgument or
		serviceReply or
		sharedSend or
		sentMessage or
		publishedValue or
		mutablePlace or
		returnedValue gives false
	end 'kind'
end 'moveKindHandsTheVarOver'

let StoreSlotValueShift = 32 as StoreSlotKey
let StoreSlotOffsetMask = u32.max as StoreSlotKey

// A container mutator stores into its first operand, and an interior insertion's second operand is the node
// it inserts beside, which it only reads (`RuntimeStoreShape`).
let RuntimeStoreReceiverIndex = 0
let RuntimeStoreAnchorIndex = 1
let RuntimeStoreSourceIndex = 1

// A mask word holds 64 roots: rank `r` is bit `r and RootBitIndexMask` of word `r shr RootWordShift`.
let RootWordShift = 6 as ElementIndex
let RootBitIndexMask = 63 as ElementIndex

// A PARAMETER trace ranks only the parameters, which fill word 0 — the summary's own bit order — so module
// `var` storage takes the first rank past them: no parameter bit can collide with it, and `storeIntoRoot`
// routes a store through it to the escaped set.
let ParameterTraceWritableRank = RootBitIndexMask + 1

// The bits of a summary's `moduleLets` word, two per read-only kind of record — a module-level
// `let`'s, a shared view's, a `let` field's, a `let` payload's, a `readonly` element's: the result
// may be or lie within one, and it may hold one. Above them, per field, payload and element kind: a
// tuple holding one, then a result that may be one; from `TupleColumnSummaryFirstBit`, one bit per
// marked tuple column.
let ResultLiesWithinAModuleLet = 1 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultHoldsAModuleLet = 2 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultLiesWithinASharedView = 4 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultHoldsASharedView = 8 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultLiesWithinALetField = 16 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultHoldsALetField = 32 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultLiesWithinALetPayload = 64 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultHoldsALetPayload = 128 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultLiesWithinAReadOnlyElement = 256 as ParamPositionMask
let ResultHoldsAReadOnlyElement = 512 as ParamPositionMask

let AliasLivenessColumns = [ProvenanceColumn.identity, ProvenanceColumn.inside]
let ViewReachColumns = [ProvenanceColumn.identity, ProvenanceColumn.inside, ProvenanceColumn.holds, ProvenanceColumn.deepHolds]
let HandedOffRecordColumns = [ProvenanceColumn.identity, ProvenanceColumn.holds, ProvenanceColumn.deepHolds]
let LetReachColumns = [ProvenanceColumn.identity, ProvenanceColumn.inside, ProvenanceColumn.holds, ProvenanceColumn.storedHolds, ProvenanceColumn.deepHolds, ProvenanceColumn.holdsWithin]
let ModuleVariableSubject = "a module variable"
let MaxFreshRounds = 16
let ReadOnlySlotKindCount = 3
let ResultProvenViewBitCount = 10
let ResultTupleKindFirstBit = ResultProvenViewBitCount
let ResultMayBeKindFirstBit = ResultTupleKindFirstBit + ReadOnlySlotKindCount
let TupleColumnSummaryFirstBit = ResultMayBeKindFirstBit + ReadOnlySlotKindCount
let TupleColumnMarkCount = RootBitIndexMask + 1 - TupleColumnSummaryFirstBit
let TupleMarkRankCount = ReadOnlySlotKindCount + TupleColumnMarkCount
let HiddenViewRankCount = ReadOnlySlotKindCount + ReadOnlySlotKindCount + TupleMarkRankCount
let EveryParamPosition = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as ParamPositionMask
let LetFieldSlotNameShift = 24 as StoreSlotKey
let SlotAccessFunctionShift = 32 as StoreSlotKey
let SlotAccessOpMask = 0xFFFFFFFF as StoreSlotKey
let NoSlotAccess = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as StoreSlotKey
let LetFieldSlotInstanceBit = 0x4000000000000000 as StoreSlotKey

enum LetSlotKind
	none
	field
	payload
end 'LetSlotKind'

enum SlotExclusivity
	pending
	exclusive
	shared
end 'SlotExclusivity'

// Ordered best to worst: `worseRecordUse` keeps the higher ordinal.
enum RecordUse
	dropped
	readOnly
	kept
end 'RecordUse'

enum WindowStep
	passes
	swapsOut
	touches
end 'WindowStep'

enum OwnerBlockScan
	untouched
	touched
	remintsTheOwner
end 'OwnerBlockScan'

enum OpShape
	slotLoad
	slotStore
	namedCall
	holdStart
	holdStop
	other
end 'OpShape'

typealias SwappedOutReturnMemo = Map with (ElementIndex, bool)
typealias SlotExclusivityMemo = Map with (StoreSlotKey, SlotExclusivity)
typealias SlotAccessHeadMap = Map with (StoreSlotKey, StoreSlotKey)
typealias LetFieldSlotMemo = Map with (StoreSlotKey, LetSlotKind)
typealias LetPayloadKindsMemo = Map with (StoreSlotKey, HeldRecordKinds)
typealias ViewSinkMap = Map with (ElementIndex, ValueId)

enum PermanenceSettling
	none
	strict
	orFresh
	strictGivenArguments
	orFreshGivenArguments
end 'PermanenceSettling'

enum RecordClaim
	soleByToken
	soleByFreshReturn
	permanent
	permanentOrFresh
	inertModuleLet
end 'RecordClaim'

union TupleColumnReach
	anyColumn
	columnAt(offset ByteOffset)
end 'TupleColumnReach'

enum PermanentView
	none
	sharedView
	letField
	letPayload
	readOnlyElement
end 'PermanentView'

module enum ArgumentKeep
	letField
	letPayload
	readOnlyElement
	mutablePlace
	consumed
end 'ArgumentKeep'

enum OperandUse
	placesEveryOperand
	placesAllButItsAddress
	placesNone
end 'OperandUse'

module typealias ArgumentKeepArray = Array with ArgumentKeep

// The sets each value carries, one root set apiece — see the table above.
enum ProvenanceColumn
	shares
	identity
	holds
	storedHolds
	deepHolds
	storedDeep
	inside
	placedWithin
	holdsWithin
end 'ProvenanceColumn'

type ViewReach
	export var viewRank as ElementIndex
	export var rootName as String
	export var rootIsParameter as bool

	static function create(viewRank ElementIndex, rootName String, rootIsParameter bool) returns Self
		return Self{viewRank: viewRank, rootName: rootName, rootIsParameter: rootIsParameter}
	end 'create'
end 'ViewReach'

// What one trace of a function found, in the summary's bit order — the row `ProvenanceSummary.widen` ORs in.
export type TracedSummaryRow
	export var shares = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var identity = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var holds = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var inside = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var holdsWithin = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var placedWithin = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var escapes = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var binds = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var letKeeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var payloadKeeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var elementKeeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var keeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var otherKeeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var recordKeeps = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var moduleLets = NoParamPositions as ParamPositionMask
	export var stores = ParamPositionMaskArray.create()
	export var deepStores = ParamPositionMaskArray.create()

	static function create() returns TracedSummaryRow
		return Self{}
	end 'create'
end 'TracedSummaryRow'

// ⭐ **A ROOT SET HOLDS ONLY ITS NONZERO WORDS.** An immutable-binding trace ranks every `let` of the function,
// so a dense mask per value would cost values × lets / 64 words — quadratic in one function's size, and nearly
// all of them zero, since a value reaches the few `let`s it was built from. A set here is a list of its nonzero
// words in ascending word order, pooled across every set of one walk, so a walk costs what its sets hold.
//
// The heads and links are concrete columns with a state column beside each, not
// `OptionalIndexColumn`s: a walk reads them in its innermost loop, where the generic column pays an
// out-of-line call and a `__retain_type_param` per read.
type RootSets
	var heads as EntryIndexArray
	var headStates as RootLinkStateArray
	var words as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var wordIndices as MaskWordCountArray
	var links as EntryIndexArray
	var linkStates as RootLinkStateArray
	var grew as bool

	static function create() returns RootSets
		return Self{heads: EntryIndexArray.create(), headStates: RootLinkStateArray.create(), words: ParamPositionMaskArray.create(), wordIndices: MaskWordCountArray.create(), links: EntryIndexArray.create(), linkStates: RootLinkStateArray.create(), grew: false}
	end 'create'

	// `setCount` empty sets, and nothing else: the pool keeps its storage, never its chunks.
	function reset(setCount ElementIndex)
		self.heads.refill(setCount, value: 0)
		self.headStates.refill(setCount, value: RootLinkState.unlinked)
		self.words.clear()
		self.wordIndices.clear()
		self.links.clear()
		self.linkStates.clear()
	end 'reset'

	function addSet() returns ElementIndex
		self.heads.push(0)
		self.headStates.push(RootLinkState.unlinked)
		return (self.heads.count() - 1) as ElementIndex
	end 'addSet'

	function first(set ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex throws AbsentError
		if (try self.headStates.get(set) otherwise panic("RootSets.first: set {set} is past the {self.headStates.count()} sets of this walk")) == RootLinkState.unlinked 'empty'
			throw AbsentError.absent
		end 'empty'

		return try self.heads.get(set) otherwise panic("RootSets.first: set {set} is past the {self.heads.count()} heads of this walk")
	end 'first'

	function hasWords(set ElementIndex) returns bool
		try self.first(set) otherwise return false
		return true
	end 'hasWords'

	function next(chunk ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex throws AbsentError
		if (try self.linkStates.get(chunk) otherwise panic("RootSets.next: chunk {chunk} is past the pool")) == RootLinkState.unlinked 'lastOfItsSet'
			throw AbsentError.absent
		end 'lastOfItsSet'

		return try self.links.get(chunk) otherwise panic("RootSets.next: chunk {chunk} is past the pool's links")
	end 'next'

	function hasNext(chunk ElementIndex) returns bool
		try self.next(chunk) otherwise return false
		return true
	end 'hasNext'

	function wordOf(chunk ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return try self.words.get(chunk) otherwise panic("RootSets.wordOf: chunk {chunk} is past the pool")
	end 'wordOf'

	function indexOf(chunk ElementIndex) returns MaskWordCount
		return try self.wordIndices.get(chunk) otherwise panic("RootSets.indexOf: chunk {chunk} is past the pool")
	end 'indexOf'

	function wordAt(set ElementIndex, word MaskWordCount) returns ParamPositionMask
		var chunk = try self.first(set) otherwise return NoParamPositions

		while self.indexOf(chunk) < word 'toTheWord'
			chunk = try self.next(chunk) otherwise return NoParamPositions
		end 'toTheWord'

		return self.wordOf(chunk) if self.indexOf(chunk) == word else NoParamPositions
	end 'wordAt'

	function hasRank(set ElementIndex, rank ElementIndex) returns bool
		return maskHasParam(self.wordAt(set, word: (rank shr RootWordShift) as MaskWordCount), param: (rank and RootBitIndexMask) as ParamCount)
	end 'hasRank'

	function addRank(set ElementIndex, rank ElementIndex)
		_ = self.orWordFrom(RootLinkSlot.setHead, at: set, index: (rank shr RootWordShift) as MaskWordCount, word: maskWithParam(NoParamPositions, param: (rank and RootBitIndexMask) as ParamCount))
	end 'addRank'

	// `to` gains every root `from` holds, in one ascending pass over both. True iff `to` grew.
	function union(to ElementIndex, from ElementIndex) returns bool
		self.grew = false

		if to == from 'itself'
			return false
		end 'itself'

		var source = try self.first(from) otherwise return false
		var slot = RootLinkSlot.setHead
		var at = to

		while true 'eachSourceWord'
			at = self.orWordFrom(slot, at: at, index: self.indexOf(source), word: self.wordOf(source))
			slot = RootLinkSlot.chunkLink
			source = try self.next(source) otherwise break
		end 'eachSourceWord'

		return self.grew
	end 'union'

	function unionWithoutRanks(to ElementIndex, from ElementIndex, firstSkipped ElementIndex, skippedCount ElementIndex) returns bool
		self.grew = false

		if to == from 'itself'
			return false
		end 'itself'

		var source = try self.first(from) otherwise return false
		var slot = RootLinkSlot.setHead
		var at = to
		let lastSkipped = firstSkipped + skippedCount - 1

		while true 'eachSourceWord'
			let wordFirstRank = (self.indexOf(source) as ElementIndex) shl RootWordShift
			var word = self.wordOf(source)

			if wordFirstRank <= lastSkipped and wordFirstRank + RootBitIndexMask >= firstSkipped 'aWordHoldingSkippedRanks'
				let firstBit = (firstSkipped - wordFirstRank) if firstSkipped > wordFirstRank else 0
				let lastBit = (lastSkipped - wordFirstRank) if lastSkipped < wordFirstRank + RootBitIndexMask else RootBitIndexMask
				word = maskWithout(word, removed: (EveryParamPosition shr (RootBitIndexMask - (lastBit - firstBit)) as ParamCount) shl firstBit as ParamCount)
			end 'aWordHoldingSkippedRanks'

			if word != NoParamPositions 'hasRanksToTake'
				at = self.orWordFrom(slot, at: at, index: self.indexOf(source), word: word)
				slot = RootLinkSlot.chunkLink
			end 'hasRanksToTake'

			source = try self.next(source) otherwise break
		end 'eachSourceWord'

		return self.grew
	end 'unionWithoutRanks'

	function orWordFrom(slot RootLinkSlot, at ElementIndex, index MaskWordCount, word ParamPositionMask) returns ElementIndex
		var beforeSlot = slot
		var before = at

		while true 'toTheWord'
			let cursor = try self.linkIn(beforeSlot, at: before) otherwise break
			let cursorIndex = self.indexOf(cursor)

			if cursorIndex == index 'present'
				let held = self.wordOf(cursor)

				if (held or word) != held 'widens'
					try self.words.set(cursor, value: held or word) otherwise panic("RootSets.orWordFrom: words.set OOB at chunk {cursor}")
					self.grew = true
				end 'widens'

				return cursor
			end 'present'

			if cursorIndex > index 'pastTheWord'
				break
			end 'pastTheWord'

			beforeSlot = RootLinkSlot.chunkLink
			before = cursor
		end 'toTheWord'

		let minted = self.words.count()
		self.words.push(word)
		self.wordIndices.push(index)

		if let following = try self.linkIn(beforeSlot, at: before) 'linksOn'
			self.links.push(following)
			self.linkStates.push(RootLinkState.linked)
		end 'linksOn' else 'endsTheSet'
			self.links.push(0)
			self.linkStates.push(RootLinkState.unlinked)
		end 'endsTheSet'

		match beforeSlot 'slot'
			setHead then self.linkHead(before, to: minted)
			chunkLink then self.linkChunk(before, to: minted)
		end 'slot'

		self.grew = true
		return minted
	end 'orWordFrom'

	function linkHead(set ElementIndex, to ElementIndex)
		try self.heads.set(set, value: to) otherwise panic("RootSets.linkHead: set {set} is past the {self.heads.count()} heads of this walk")
		try self.headStates.set(set, value: RootLinkState.linked) otherwise panic("RootSets.linkHead: set {set} is past the {self.headStates.count()} sets of this walk")
	end 'linkHead'

	function linkChunk(chunk ElementIndex, to ElementIndex)
		try self.links.set(chunk, value: to) otherwise panic("RootSets.linkChunk: chunk {chunk} is past the pool's links")
		try self.linkStates.set(chunk, value: RootLinkState.linked) otherwise panic("RootSets.linkChunk: chunk {chunk} is past the pool")
	end 'linkChunk'

	function linkIn(slot RootLinkSlot, at ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex throws AbsentError
		match slot 'slot'
			setHead then return try self.first(at)
			chunkLink then return try self.next(at)
		end 'slot'
	end 'linkIn'
end 'RootSets'

// What each function's RESULT is to its own parameters, by function index, and where its body STORES them:
// into a field of another parameter's record (`storesInto`, one mask per receiving parameter), deeper inside
// it (`storesDeep`), into module storage (`escapes`) — and which it BINDS to a mutable name that outlives the
// call, a module `var` or a by-reference parameter's cell (`binds`). `moduleLets` is what the result is to the
// records module-level `let`s hold, in `ResultLiesWithinAModuleLet` and `ResultHoldsAModuleLet` bits.
// `otherKeeps` is the part of `keeps` kept somewhere other than the result, and `recordKeeps` the
// part of `keeps` and `binds` kept as a record of its own type rather than only as a type
// parameter's content.
export type ProvenanceSummary
	var shares as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var identity as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var holds as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var inside as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var holdsWithin as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var placedWithin as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var escapes as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var binds as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var letKeeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var payloadKeeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var elementKeeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var keeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var otherKeeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var recordKeeps as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var moduleLets as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var storesInto as ParamMaskRows
	var storesDeep as ParamMaskRows
	var noStoredParameters as ParamPositionMaskArray

	export static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns ProvenanceSummary
		var noStoredParameters = ParamPositionMaskArray.create()

		return Self{shares: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), identity: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), holds: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), inside: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), holdsWithin: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), placedWithin: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), escapes: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), binds: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), letKeeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), payloadKeeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), elementKeeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), keeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), otherKeeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), recordKeeps: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), moduleLets: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), storesInto: emptyStoreRows(funcCount, sharedEmptyRow: noStoredParameters), storesDeep: emptyStoreRows(funcCount, sharedEmptyRow: noStoredParameters), noStoredParameters: noStoredParameters}
	end 'create'

	export function resultMayReachAModuleLet(index ElementIndex) returns bool
		return self.moduleLetsAt(index) != NoParamPositions
	end 'resultMayReachAModuleLet'

	export function moduleLetsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.moduleLets, index: index)
	end 'moduleLetsAt'

	export function sharesAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.shares, index: index)
	end 'sharesAt'

	export function identityAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.identity, index: index)
	end 'identityAt'

	export function holdsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.holds, index: index)
	end 'holdsAt'

	export function insideAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.inside, index: index)
	end 'insideAt'

	export function holdsWithinAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.holdsWithin, index: index)
	end 'holdsWithinAt'

	export function placedWithinAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.placedWithin, index: index)
	end 'placedWithinAt'

	export function escapesAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.escapes, index: index)
	end 'escapesAt'

	export function letKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.letKeeps, index: index)
	end 'letKeepsAt'

	export function payloadKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.payloadKeeps, index: index)
	end 'payloadKeepsAt'

	export function elementKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.elementKeeps, index: index)
	end 'elementKeepsAt'

	export function anyKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return self.letKeepsAt(index) or self.payloadKeepsAt(index) or self.elementKeepsAt(index)
	end 'anyKeepsAt'

	export function keepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.keeps, index: index)
	end 'keepsAt'

	export function otherKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.otherKeeps, index: index)
	end 'otherKeepsAt'

	export function recordKeepsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.recordKeeps, index: index)
	end 'recordKeepsAt'

	export function bindsAt(index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
		return summaryMaskAt(self.binds, index: index)
	end 'bindsAt'

	// The parameters function `index` stores into a field of parameter `into`'s record.
	export function storesAt(index ElementIndex, into ParamCount) returns ParamPositionMask
		return storeRowMaskAt(self.storesInto, index: index, into: into)
	end 'storesAt'

	// The parameters function `index` stores deeper inside parameter `into`'s record.
	export function storesDeepAt(index ElementIndex, into ParamCount) returns ParamPositionMask
		return storeRowMaskAt(self.storesDeep, index: index, into: into)
	end 'storesDeepAt'

	// Widen function `index` by what one trace of it found. True iff a mask grew — the only event that can
	// change a caller's answer.
	export function widen(index ElementIndex, row TracedSummaryRow) returns bool
		var grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.shares, index: index, by: row.shares)
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.identity, index: index, by: row.identity) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.holds, index: index, by: row.holds) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.inside, index: index, by: row.inside) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.holdsWithin, index: index, by: row.holdsWithin) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.placedWithin, index: index, by: row.placedWithin) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.escapes, index: index, by: row.escapes) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.binds, index: index, by: row.binds) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.letKeeps, index: index, by: row.letKeeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.payloadKeeps, index: index, by: row.payloadKeeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.elementKeeps, index: index, by: row.elementKeeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.keeps, index: index, by: row.keeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.otherKeeps, index: index, by: row.otherKeeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.recordKeeps, index: index, by: row.recordKeeps) or grew
		grew = widenSummaryColumn(self.moduleLets, index: index, by: row.moduleLets) or grew
		grew = widenStoreRow(self.storesInto, index: index, by: row.stores, sharedEmptyRow: self.noStoredParameters) or grew
		grew = widenStoreRow(self.storesDeep, index: index, by: row.deepStores, sharedEmptyRow: self.noStoredParameters) or grew
		return grew
	end 'widen'
end 'ProvenanceSummary'

module function emptyStoreRows(funcCount ElementIndex, sharedEmptyRow ParamPositionMaskArray) returns ParamMaskRows
	var rows = ParamMaskRows.create()
	rows.refill(funcCount, value: sharedEmptyRow)
	return rows
end 'emptyStoreRows'

// A row shorter than `into` is one no store has reached that far along.
module function storeRowMaskAt(rows ParamMaskRows, index ElementIndex, into ParamCount) returns ParamPositionMask
	let row = try rows.get(index) otherwise panic("ProvenanceSummary: function index {index} is outside the store rows — they are built over `funcNames.functions`")
	return try row.get(into) otherwise NoParamPositions
end 'storeRowMaskAt'

module function widenStoreRow(rows ParamMaskRows, index ElementIndex, by ParamPositionMaskArray, sharedEmptyRow ParamPositionMaskArray) returns bool
	var row = try rows.get(index) otherwise panic("widenStoreRow: function index {index} is outside the store rows — they are built over `funcNames.functions`")
	var grew = false

	for into in 0 upto by.count() 'eachReceivingParameter'
		let stored = try by.get(into) otherwise panic("widenStoreRow: by.get OOB at {into}")

		if stored == NoParamPositions 'nothingStoredHere'
			continue
		end 'nothingStoredHere'

		if row is sharedEmptyRow 'firstStore'
			row = ParamPositionMaskArray.create()
			row.refill(by.count(), value: NoParamPositions)
			try rows.set(index, value: row) otherwise panic("widenStoreRow: rows.set OOB at {index}")
		end 'firstStore'

		let before = try row.get(into) otherwise panic("widenStoreRow: row of function {index} is shorter than its {by.count()} parameters")

		if (before or stored) != before 'widens'
			try row.set(into, value: before or stored) otherwise panic("widenStoreRow: row.set OOB at {into}")
			grew = true
		end 'widens'
	end 'eachReceivingParameter'

	return grew
end 'widenStoreRow'

module function emptySummaryColumn(funcCount ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMaskArray
	var column = ParamPositionMaskArray.create()
	column.refill(funcCount, value: NoParamPositions)
	return column
end 'emptySummaryColumn'

// By function index, the parameters a receiver-writing call writes through a value that may BE their record
// (`identity`), and through one that may only lie WITHIN it (`within`) — `buildParamMutationSummary` seeds
// different columns from each.
export type ProvenanceReceiverWrites
	export var identity as ParamPositionMaskArray
	export var within as ParamPositionMaskArray

	static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns ProvenanceReceiverWrites
		return Self{identity: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), within: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount)}
	end 'create'
end 'ProvenanceReceiverWrites'

module function summaryMaskAt(column ParamPositionMaskArray, index ElementIndex) returns ParamPositionMask
	return try column.get(index) otherwise panic("ProvenanceSummary: function index {index} is outside the column — it is built over `funcNames.functions`")
end 'summaryMaskAt'

module function widenSummaryColumn(column ParamPositionMaskArray, index ElementIndex, by ParamPositionMask) returns bool
	let before = summaryMaskAt(column, index: index)
	let after = before or by

	if after == before 'nothingNew'
		return false
	end 'nothingNew'

	try column.set(index, value: after) otherwise panic("ProvenanceSummary.widen: set OOB at {index}")
	return true
end 'widenSummaryColumn'

// ⭐ **THE SUMMARY IS A LEAST FIXPOINT OVER THE CALL GRAPH**, for `buildParamMutationSummary`'s reason: a
// callee may be declared after its caller, or be it. Every function with a parameter or a result that can hold a
// record is traced once, recording the callees it consulted; then the callers of every function whose masks grew
// are traced again until nothing grows. Masks only gain bits, so the re-traces are bounded by the call edges times
// the mask width.
//
// ⭐ **A CALLER IS RE-TRACED ONLY WHILE STALE** — while a summary it consults has grown since its last trace
// began. Its dependency rows repeat per call site and per pass of its walk, and a trace whose every input is
// as it last read them answers the masks it already widened by, so skipping it leaves every summary exactly
// as tracing it would.
module function buildStorageProvenance(project Project, module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, funcNames FunctionNameIndex, summaryIndex CallSummaryIndex) returns ProvenanceTracer throws CompileError
	let funcCount = funcNames.functions.count()
	var tracer = ProvenanceTracer.create(project, module: module, signatures: signatures, calls: CallSiteCursor.create(summaryIndex), funcCount: funcCount)
	try settleSummaries(project, order: calleesFirstOrder(module, funcNames: funcNames), bodies: tracer, dependencies: tracer.calls.dependencies)
	tracer.markBodiesHandedAModuleLetsRecord(funcNames)
	tracer.settleFreshReturns(funcNames)
	tracer.settlePermanentReturns(funcNames)
	return tracer
end 'buildStorageProvenance'

// A run of rows filed for one function in a column every function appends to — the calls a walk resolves
// and the parameter edges a trace files are both held that way, so the range bookkeeping and the one mark
// for "nothing filed for this function yet" are written once.
module enum FunctionRowsLookup implements Error
	unfiled
end 'FunctionRowsLookup'

export type FunctionRows
	var firstRows as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var stopRows as OptionalElementIndexColumn

	export static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns FunctionRows
		return Self{firstRows: OptionalElementIndexColumn.absent(funcCount), stopRows: OptionalElementIndexColumn.absent(funcCount)}
	end 'create'

	// `funcIndex`'s rows are `[firstRow, stopRow)`. Filing again replaces the range, which is what a
	// re-trace does.
	export function file(funcIndex ElementIndex, firstRow ElementIndex, stopRow ElementIndex)
		self.requireFunction(funcIndex)
		self.firstRows.set(funcIndex, value: firstRow)
		self.stopRows.set(funcIndex, value: stopRow)
	end 'file'

	module function firstRowOf(funcIndex ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex throws FunctionRowsLookup
		self.requireFunction(funcIndex)
		return try self.firstRows.get(funcIndex) otherwise throw FunctionRowsLookup.unfiled
	end 'firstRowOf'

	export function unfileEvery()
		self.firstRows.makeAbsent(self.firstRows.count())
		self.stopRows.makeAbsent(self.stopRows.count())
	end 'unfileEvery'

	export function stopRowOf(funcIndex ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex
		self.requireFunction(funcIndex)
		return try self.stopRows.get(funcIndex) otherwise panic("FunctionRows.stopRowOf: nothing is filed for function {funcIndex} — a caller reads the first row before the stop")
	end 'stopRowOf'

	function requireFunction(funcIndex ElementIndex)
		if funcIndex >= self.firstRows.count() 'pastTheFunctions'
			panic("FunctionRows: function {funcIndex} is past the tracer's function count")
		end 'pastTheFunctions'
	end 'requireFunction'
end 'FunctionRows'

typealias RuntimeStoreShapeArray = Array with RuntimeStoreShape

// ⭐ **EACH TRACED BODY'S CALLS AS A WALK READS THEM, RESOLVED ON THE BODY'S FIRST WALK AND KEYED BY ITS
// FUNCTION INDEX.** A call's callee and labels do not change while the tracer lives, and a walk meets every
// call of a body at every pass of every trace — and `stageParamEdges` meets them again — so answering by
// name at each meeting (the function and signature indexes, the labels against the parameter names, the
// runtime rosters' comparisons) pays many times over for one answer.
//
// A body's rows are its `FunctionRows` range, in the order every pass of a walk meets its calls. A row is
// DESCRIBED when a summary answers for its callee (`summarizedCalleeIndex`) and then names an entry
// of the described columns; otherwise it names an entry of the runtime columns.
export type CallSites
	export var ranges as FunctionRows
	var described as BoolArray
	var entries as EntryIndexArray

	// A described callee's index, and each argument's parameter position and whether it fills one, from
	// `argStarts`.
	var callees as FuncIndexArray
	var argStarts as EntryIndexArray
	var argPositions as ParamCountArray
	var argFills as BoolArray

	// A callee no summary describes: where it may store what it was handed, and the runtime families it belongs to.
	var shapes as RuntimeStoreShapeArray
	var bookkeeping as BoolArray
	var linksANewNode as BoolArray

	export static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns CallSites
		return Self{ranges: FunctionRows.create(funcCount), described: BoolArray.create(), entries: EntryIndexArray.create(), callees: FuncIndexArray.create(), argStarts: EntryIndexArray.create(), argPositions: ParamCountArray.create(), argFills: BoolArray.create(), shapes: RuntimeStoreShapeArray.create(), bookkeeping: BoolArray.create(), linksANewNode: BoolArray.create()}
	end 'create'

	export function nextRow() returns ElementIndex
		return self.described.count()
	end 'nextRow'

	export function closeRows(funcIndex ElementIndex, firstRow ElementIndex)
		self.ranges.file(funcIndex, firstRow: firstRow, stopRow: self.described.count())
	end 'closeRows'

	export function fileDescribedRow(calleeIndex ElementIndex, slottedArgs ParamCountArray, fills BoolArray)
		self.described.push(true)
		self.entries.push(self.callees.count())
		self.callees.push(calleeIndex)
		self.argStarts.push(self.argPositions.count())
		self.argPositions.append(slottedArgs)
		self.argFills.append(fills)
	end 'fileDescribedRow'

	export function fileRuntimeRow(shape RuntimeStoreShape, isBookkeeping bool, linksANode bool)
		self.described.push(false)
		self.entries.push(self.shapes.count())
		self.shapes.push(shape)
		self.bookkeeping.push(isBookkeeping)
		self.linksANewNode.push(linksANode)
	end 'fileRuntimeRow'

	export function rowIsDescribed(row ElementIndex) returns bool
		return try self.described.get(row) otherwise panic("CallSites.rowIsDescribed: described.get OOB at call-site row {row}")
	end 'rowIsDescribed'

	function entryAt(row ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex
		return try self.entries.get(row) otherwise panic("CallSites.entryAt: entries.get OOB at call-site row {row}")
	end 'entryAt'

	export function calleeAt(row ElementIndex) returns ElementIndex
		return try self.callees.get(self.entryAt(row)) otherwise panic("CallSites.calleeAt: callees.get OOB at described call-site row {row}")
	end 'calleeAt'

	export function argPositionAt(row ElementIndex, argIndex ParamCount) returns ParamCount throws MapError
		let at = (try self.argStarts.get(self.entryAt(row)) otherwise panic("CallSites.argPositionAt: argStarts.get OOB at described call-site row {row}")) + argIndex

		if not (try self.argFills.get(at) otherwise panic("CallSites.argPositionAt: argFills.get OOB at {at}")) 'fillsNoParameter'
			throw MapError.keyNotFound
		end 'fillsNoParameter'

		return try self.argPositions.get(at) otherwise panic("CallSites.argPositionAt: argPositions.get OOB at {at}")
	end 'argPositionAt'

	export function shapeAt(row ElementIndex) returns RuntimeStoreShape
		return try self.shapes.get(self.entryAt(row)) otherwise panic("CallSites.shapeAt: shapes.get OOB at runtime call-site row {row}")
	end 'shapeAt'

	export function isBookkeepingAt(row ElementIndex) returns bool
		return try self.bookkeeping.get(self.entryAt(row)) otherwise panic("CallSites.isBookkeepingAt: bookkeeping.get OOB at runtime call-site row {row}")
	end 'isBookkeepingAt'

	export function linksANewNodeAt(row ElementIndex) returns bool
		return try self.linksANewNode.get(self.entryAt(row)) otherwise panic("CallSites.linksANewNodeAt: linksANewNode.get OOB at runtime call-site row {row}")
	end 'linksANewNodeAt'
end 'CallSites'

// ⭐ **EACH BODY'S PARAMETER RECORD EDGES, AS ITS LAST PARAMETER TRACE REACHED THEM.** Filed after every
// trace the fixpoint makes, so `collectProvenanceParamEdges` needs no trace of its own — see
// `StagedParamEdges` for why the last one is the trace that pass wants.
//
// A re-trace appends its rows and leaves the ones it replaced in the log. MEASURED on this compiler: the log
// ends at 3,543 identity rows and 59,230 record rows, of which 999 and 22,198 are live — ~2 MB, and ~1.3 MB
// of that superseded. Compacting the log costs more than it holds (+1,351 allocations and +6.1 MB over a
// whole compile), so the log is kept whole and RELEASED once that pass has read it.
export type StagedEdgeRows
	export var rows as CallParamEdges
	var ranges as FunctionRows

	export static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns StagedEdgeRows
		return Self{rows: CallParamEdges.create(), ranges: FunctionRows.create(funcCount)}
	end 'create'

	// `index`'s rows are those appended to the log since `start`, which replaces the range an earlier trace
	// of the same body filed.
	export function file(index ElementIndex, start CsrIndex)
		self.ranges.file(index, firstRow: start, stopRow: self.rows.count())
	end 'file'

	// The rows `index`'s last trace filed — none for a body no trace filed any for, which is every body
	// with no record parameter.
	export function appendRowsOf(index ElementIndex, into CallParamEdges)
		let first = try self.ranges.firstRowOf(index) otherwise return
		into.appendRowsIn(self.rows, firstRow: first as CsrIndex, stopRow: self.ranges.stopRowOf(index) as CsrIndex)
	end 'appendRowsOf'

	// The log is read once, so it is dropped there rather than held to the end of `semanticCheck`.
	export function release()
		self.rows = CallParamEdges.create()
		self.ranges.unfileEvery()
	end 'release'
end 'StagedEdgeRows'

// ⭐ **THE FIXPOINT'S LAST TRACE OF A BODY IS THE TRACE `collectProvenanceParamEdges` WANTS.** A body is
// traced again whenever a summary it consults grows (`markCallersStale`), so its last trace read every
// callee's settled summary — which is what that pass used to re-trace every body to obtain. Staging after
// each trace costs one walk of the body's ops; re-tracing every body costs a fixpoint walk of each.
//
// A body with no record parameter is staged by no trace and reads back as empty here, which is the answer
// that pass wants for it: the fixpoint's first pass traces every body that HAS one.
export type StagedParamEdges
	export var alias as StagedEdgeRows
	export var within as StagedEdgeRows
	export var written as ParamPositionMaskArray
	export var writtenWithin as ParamPositionMaskArray

	export static function create(funcCount ElementIndex) returns StagedParamEdges
		return Self{alias: StagedEdgeRows.create(funcCount), within: StagedEdgeRows.create(funcCount), written: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount), writtenWithin: emptySummaryColumn(funcCount)}
	end 'create'

	export function file(index ElementIndex, aliasStart CsrIndex, withinStart CsrIndex, receiverWritten ParamPositionMask, receiverWrittenWithin ParamPositionMask)
		self.alias.file(index, start: aliasStart)
		self.within.file(index, start: withinStart)
		try self.written.set(index, value: receiverWritten) otherwise panic("StagedParamEdges.file: written.set OOB at function {index}")
		try self.writtenWithin.set(index, value: receiverWrittenWithin) otherwise panic("StagedParamEdges.file: writtenWithin.set OOB at function {index}")
	end 'file'

	export function release()
		self.alias.release()
		self.within.release()
	end 'release'
end 'StagedParamEdges'

union IndexedFunctionBody
	none
	body(let name ByteArray)

	function isOf(name ByteArray) returns bool
		return match self 'indexed'
			none gives false
			body(indexed) gives indexed.equals(name)
		end 'indexed'
	end 'isOf'
end 'IndexedFunctionBody'

// `unwritten` is still a call: its result may share what it was handed (`accessRootOfStop`), and only its
// wording is unattributed.
union CallProducer
	written(let wording String)
	unwritten
	notACall

	function isACall() returns bool
		return match self 'producer'
			written or
			unwritten gives true
			notACall gives false
		end 'producer'
	end 'isACall'

	function subject() returns String
		return match self 'producer'
			written(wording) gives wording
			unwritten or
			notACall gives UnattributedProducer
		end 'producer'
	end 'subject'
end 'CallProducer'

union AccessRoot
	binding(let rank ElementIndex)
	computed
	ground
	unknown
end 'AccessRoot'

enum WriteDoor
	aReceiver
	aTarget
end 'WriteDoor'

// ⭐ **ONE FUNCTION'S PROVENANCE WALK, and the scratch it reuses across every function it walks.** Each value
// holds one root set per `ProvenanceColumn`, one bit per root; a walk iterates the body until no set grows,
// which a loop's back edge needs and a straight-line body settles in one extra pass.
module type ProvenanceTracer implements SummaryCallWalker, SummarizedBodies
	var project as Project
	var module as MaxonModule
	var signatures as ProgramSignatures
	export var calls as CallSiteCursor
	var stagedEdges as StagedParamEdges
	export var summary as ProvenanceSummary

	// Value `v`'s set in column `c` is `c.ordinal * setsPerColumn + v`, one per value; a store slot's set
	// follows them. `columnCount` is read once, because `allCases` builds an array at every read.
	var sets as RootSets
	let columnCount as ElementIndex
	var setsPerColumn as ElementIndex

	// What each `(address, offset)` was handed, and what was stored inside the record a load of it yields
	// (`deepSlots`, keyed by the load's own `(address, offset)`, which `loadOrigins` keeps per loaded value).
	var storeSlots as StoreSlotTable
	var deepSlots as StoreSlotTable
	var loadOrigins as StoreSlotKeyArray
	var hasLoadOrigin as BoolArray
	var tracked as BoolArray
	var namedTypeHoldsARecord as NamedTypeRecordMemo
	var namedTypeIsUnwritable as NamedTypeRecordMemo
	var rootValues as ValueIdArray

	// The `let` bindings' names, by rank: an immutable-binding trace ranks them first, so a rank is a binding's
	// exactly when it is below this column's count. The parameters follow them there, then writable storage.
	var rootNames as NameRoster

	// By rank, the kinds of record that may lie within a root's record — a binding's or a parameter's.
	var rootRecordKinds as HeldRecordKindsArray
	var recordKindsByAggregate as AggregateRecordKindsMemo
	var recordKindsByInstance as InstanceRecordKindsMemo
	var noRecordKinds as HeldRecordKinds
	var anyRecordKinds as HeldRecordKinds
	var rootRankOfValue as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var tracingImmutableBindings as bool
	var writableRank as ElementIndex

	// Which values a `var` binding holds: the door that bound it (E3078) answers for a write through one, so
	// E3159 at an argument leaves it alone.
	var isWritableValue as BoolArray
	var isImmutableBindingValue as BoolArray

	// By rank, for an immutable-binding trace: whether a binding root is a module-level `let`, whether
	// a second `let` names its very value, its binding record and declaration token, how far it stays
	// live (`rootLiveUntil`), whether its record is its own (`rootSoleBase`), and the earliest door
	// that moved it.
	var rootIsModuleLet as BoolArray

	// The last use of each root through a second name for its record (`let u = t`), which keeps it live as its own does.
	var rootAliasLastUse as TokenIndexArray
	var rootAliased as BoolArray
	var rootInfos as VarInfoArray
	var rootDeclTokens as TokenIndexArray
	var rootLiveUntil as TokenIndexArray
	var rootSoleBase as BoolArray
	var rootMovedAt as TokenIndexArray

	// By rank, whether a closure literal captured the binding: the closure reads it wherever it is called.
	var rootCaptured as BoolArray

	// By value, the rank of a `var`'s own record in an immutable-binding trace — one each, so two
	// reads out of one `var` can be told to lie within the same storage (E3078, E3188, E3159).
	var writableRankOfValue as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var firstWritableValueRank as ElementIndex

	// By word, the ranks that are storage something may write: every `var`'s record but an iterator's,
	// module `var` storage and a parameter the body writes. `callWrittenPlaceWords` adds a parameter a
	// call writes, and a `let` reaching a rank there is bound to writable state (E3188).
	var mutablePlaceWords as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var callWrittenPlaceWords as ParamPositionMaskArray

	// By word, the ranks of an immutable-binding trace that are parameters.
	var parameterRankWords as ParamPositionMaskArray

	// ⭐ **THE DOOR BEING ASKED ABOUT** (`askAtDoor`). A root moved by it or not live after it does not
	// count there (`rootCountsAtDoor`, `varGoneBeforeDoor`); `NoDoorToken` asks with no door's
	// liveness.
	var doorToken as ElementIndex

	// The `.data` labels of the `let` globals, whose `globalAddr` is module storage no write reaches.
	var immutableGlobalLabels as GlobalDataLabelSet

	// Every kind of record a module-level `let` is or holds, at any depth.
	var moduleLetRecordKinds as HeldRecordKinds

	// Everything a store put where module storage holds it: a parameter trace's `escapes`.
	var escapedSet as ElementIndex
	var operands as ValueIdArray

	// One function's refusals, reported in source order once every door has asked.
	var refusals as PendingRefusalArray

	// Per argument of the call `argumentsReachAParameter` last asked about, the parameters it may be the record of
	// and the parameters it may lie within.
	var argIdentityReach as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var argWithinReach as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var changed as bool

	var returnedShares as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedIdentity as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedHolds as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedInside as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedHoldsWithin as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedPlacedWithin as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedEscapes as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedBinds as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedLetKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedPayloadKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedElementKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedOtherKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var returnedRecordKeeps as ParamPositionMask
	var writtenMasks as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var recordWrittenMasks as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var letRefused as BoolArray
	var keptRefusedValues as ValueIdArray
	var keptRefusedAt as PositionKeyArray
	var keptSiteHeads as KeptSiteHeadsByCall
	var keptSiteNext as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var keptSitesValid as bool
	var keptSitesIndex as ElementIndex
	var landingKeeps as LandingKeeps
	var letCheckedValid as bool
	var letCheckedIndex as ElementIndex
	var opaqueBoundBodies as BoolArray
	var returnedModuleLets as ParamPositionMask

	// Whether a call of the walk being traced handed back a value that may reach a module-level `let`'s record.
	var moduleLetStorageReached as bool

	// By function, whether a call of its body may hand it a module-level `let`'s record
	// (`markBodiesHandedAModuleLetsRecord`).
	var handedAModuleLetsRecord as BoolArray
	var storedRow as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var storedDeepRow as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var capturedPositions as CapturedLoadMap
	var rankCount as ParamCount

	// E3159's per-argument question (`immutableRootWrittenThrough`) is asked of the function `checkCalls` has entered,
	// and traced once for it however many of its arguments ask.
	var enteredIndex as ElementIndex
	var bindingsTraceValid as bool
	var bindingsTraceIndex as ElementIndex
	var bindingsRootCount as ElementIndex

	// The parameters receiver-writing calls write through values that may be or lie within their records
	// (`stageParamEdges`).
	export var receiverWrites as ProvenanceReceiverWrites

	// Every argument a call hands to a parameter its callee writes, by the function the call is in —
	// in function order, since `checkCalls` asks a function's doors (`checkFunctionDoors`) once it has
	// walked its calls — and, for the function being asked about, every rank a value a write goes
	// through may be: those, receivers and field-written boxes, as one set, so a `var` asks it once
	// rather than once per write.
	var writtenArgFuncs as FuncIndexArray
	var writtenArgValues as ValueIdArray
	var writtenArgCalls as SourceRangeArray
	var writtenArgParams as ArgumentParameterArray
	var writtenArgJudged as BoolArray
	var writtenArgsHere as EntryIndexArray
	var landingNotedPositions as ParamCountArray
	var landingNotedRows as EntryIndexArray

	var keptArgFuncs as FuncIndexArray
	var keptArgValues as ValueIdArray
	var keptArgCalls as SourceRangeArray
	var keptArgParams as ArgumentParameterArray
	var keptArgCallees as NameRoster
	var keptArgCursor as ElementIndex

	// Every rank a refused `var` door took over — the `var`'s own record, and a name it was handed whole — so a
	// write through that record is not refused a second time: the door that bound it already was.
	var refusedDoorRanks as ElementIndex
	var pendingKeeps as PendingKeepArray
	var refusedBodies as BoolArray
	var returnedValues as ValueIdArray
	var keptEscapes as BoolArray
	var keptReturned as BoolArray
	var functionHoldings as FunctionHoldingAnswers
	var keptEverythingEscapes as bool
	var varMovedAt as TokenIndexArray
	var varDeadFrom as TokenIndexArray
	var keptRefusedRanks as ElementIndex

	// Each binding root's reads, by rank: `rootReads` from `rootReadStarts[rank]` up to `rootReadStarts[rank + 1]`.
	var rootReadStarts as EntryIndexArray
	var rootReads as TokenIndexArray
	var tracedSites as ProvenanceSites

	// What a function that filed no provenance answers (`IrFunction.provenanceSites`).
	var noSites as ProvenanceSites
	var refusedDoorValues as BoolArray

	// Per value of the function `indexedDefinitionsOf` names: the op that defines it, the hop that op takes toward the
	// record the value was read out of (`indexDefinition`, by kind, base and step), and — for a merge — the one value
	// every edge into it hands it (`soleIncomingValue`). Built once per function asked, so a question along an access
	// path reads columns rather than scanning the body.
	var indexedDefinitionsOf as IndexedFunctionBody
	var definingOps as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var mergingBlocks as MergingBlockColumn
	var hopKinds as AccessHopKindArray
	var hopBases as ValueIdArray
	var hopSteps as AccessStepColumn
	var soleIncomings as ValueIdArray
	var soleIncomingSeen as BoolArray
	var incomingStart as EntryIndexArray
	var incomingLength as EntryIndexArray
	var incomingComplete as BoolArray
	var incomingValues as ValueIdArray
	var pairMerge as ValueIdArray
	var pairIncoming as ValueIdArray
	var pairHanded as BoolArray
	var blockPairStart as EntryIndexArray
	var useCounts as EntryIndexArray
	var useCountsIndexed = false

	// Scratch the write-time questions reuse from one question to the next: the two access paths compared, the records
	// stored into the two fields compared, the arguments a call is handed a record at, the fill of each root's reads,
	// and the reachability walk's worklist and visited blocks.
	var pathSteps as PathStepArray
	var rootReadFill as EntryIndexArray
	var reachWorklist as BlockIdArray
	var reachVisited as BoolArray
	var writtenArgCursor as ElementIndex
	var writtenRanks as ElementIndex
	var writtenWithinRanks as ElementIndex

	// Where each binding-hygiene diagnostic sits, by its position — the first at a position, and the next at the same
	// one in `hygieneNextAtPosition` — indexed at the first E3077 a door settles (`hygieneIndexOf`), and which of them
	// a door withdrew (`dropWithdrawnHygiene`).
	var hygieneIndexed as bool
	var hygieneFirstAtPosition as HygieneIndexByPosition
	var hygieneNextAtPosition as OptionalElementIndexColumn
	var hygieneWithdrawn as BoolArray

	// What the last trace found, refilled by every widening (`widenSummary`).
	var summaryRow as TracedSummaryRow

	// Each block of the function `indexedDefinitionsOf` names by its id, refilled with the rest of that index
	// (`indexDefinitions`).
	var blockIndex as BlockIndexById

	// The calls `callTokenAtPosition` last indexed, and their token and start indexes.
	var indexedCalls as CallTokenColumns
	var callTokenIndex as TokenByPosition
	var callStartIndex as StartByPosition

	var freshReturns as BoolArray
	var freshMember as BoolArray
	var freshRequired as BoolArray
	var freshChecked as BoolArray
	var freshChanged as bool
	var freshNeeds as FuncIndexArray
	var letFieldSlots as LetFieldSlotMemo
	var letPayloadKinds as LetPayloadKindsMemo
	var keptArgKinds as ArgumentKeepArray
	var viewSinks as ViewSinkMap
	var permanentReturns as BoolArray
	var permanentNeeds as FuncIndexArray
	var permanentOrFreshReturns as BoolArray
	var permanentSettling as PermanenceSettling
	var permanentGivenReturns as BoolArray
	var permanentOrFreshGivenReturns as BoolArray
	var permanentGivenParams as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var permanentOrFreshGivenParams as ParamPositionMaskArray
	var permanentParamsNeeded as ParamPositionMask
	var permanentUsedGiven as bool
	var inertGlobalLabels as GlobalDataLabelSet
	var slotExclusivity as SlotExclusivityMemo
	var slotAccessHeads as SlotAccessHeadMap
	var slotAccessPacked as StoreSlotKeyArray
	var slotAccessNext as StoreSlotKeyArray
	var slotAccessesIndexed as bool
	var slotAccessedThroughAnUnkeyedAddress as bool
	var moduleVarKinds as HeldRecordKinds
	var swapOperands as ValueIdArray
	var aliasesGrew as bool
	var swappedOutReturns as SwappedOutReturnMemo
	var valueHandedOut as BoolArray
	var handedOutComputed as bool
	var readOnlyKeptBases as ValueIdArray
	var readOnlyKeptAt as PositionKeyArray
	var doorAcceptsParameters as bool

	static function create(project Project, module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, calls CallSiteCursor, funcCount ElementIndex) returns ProvenanceTracer
		var noSites = ProvenanceSites.create(ProvenanceColumns.create())
		return Self{project: project, module: module, signatures: signatures, calls: calls, stagedEdges: StagedParamEdges.create(funcCount), summary: ProvenanceSummary.create(funcCount), sets: RootSets.create(), columnCount: ProvenanceColumn.allCases.count(), setsPerColumn: 0, storeSlots: StoreSlotTable.create(), deepSlots: StoreSlotTable.create(), loadOrigins: StoreSlotKeyArray.create(), hasLoadOrigin: BoolArray.create(), tracked: BoolArray.create(), namedTypeHoldsARecord: NamedTypeRecordMemo.create(), namedTypeIsUnwritable: NamedTypeRecordMemo.create(), rootValues: ValueIdArray.create(), rootNames: NameRoster.create(), rootRecordKinds: HeldRecordKindsArray.create(), recordKindsByAggregate: AggregateRecordKindsMemo.create(), recordKindsByInstance: InstanceRecordKindsMemo.create(), noRecordKinds: HeldRecordKinds.create(), anyRecordKinds: anyHeldRecordKinds(), rootRankOfValue: OptionalElementIndexColumn.create(), tracingImmutableBindings: false, writableRank: ParameterTraceWritableRank, isWritableValue: BoolArray.create(), isImmutableBindingValue: BoolArray.create(), rootIsModuleLet: BoolArray.create(), rootAliasLastUse: TokenIndexArray.create(), rootAliased: BoolArray.create(), rootInfos: VarInfoArray.create(), rootDeclTokens: TokenIndexArray.create(), rootLiveUntil: TokenIndexArray.create(), rootSoleBase: BoolArray.create(), rootMovedAt: TokenIndexArray.create(), rootCaptured: BoolArray.create(), writableRankOfValue: OptionalElementIndexColumn.create(), firstWritableValueRank: 0, mutablePlaceWords: ParamPositionMaskArray.create(), callWrittenPlaceWords: ParamPositionMaskArray.create(), parameterRankWords: ParamPositionMaskArray.create(), doorToken: NoDoorToken, immutableGlobalLabels: signatures.immutableGlobalDataLabels(), moduleLetRecordKinds: moduleLetKindsOf(project, signatures: signatures), escapedSet: 0, operands: ValueIdArray.create(), refusals: PendingRefusalArray.create(), argIdentityReach: ParamPositionMaskArray.create(), argWithinReach: ParamPositionMaskArray.c